url: "https://sinusoidal-history.skylarkcreations.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/u00dxk2/sinusoidal-history"
abstract: >-
  Sinusoidal History overlays eight named long-wave theories of history
  (Khaldun, Kondratiev, Huntington, Schlesinger Jr., Perez, Turchin, Dalio,
  Strauss-Howe) on a shared 1600–2050 time axis as unit-amplitude sinusoids,
  each pinned to one explicitly documented reference peak. Seven of the
  eight cycles are paired with a real long-run empirical data series for
  stress-testing. The site is an editorial comparison tool, not a forecasting
  instrument: it makes the role of calibration, theorist motivation, and
  selection effect visible by construction. Data sources are documented on
  the site's /methods page; per-source provenance is committed alongside
  each CSV.
keywords:
  - long-wave theory
  - cliodynamics
